    "md5": "c81a27e1d29ca654bd810442386c39e6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1378,
    "chunk_text": "Hon. Friends, I want to put on record that His Excellency the Prime Minister of India directly told the IMF, \u201cIf you are not willing to give US Dollars 2.6 billion as the IMF standby credit facility to Sri Lanka, we, the Indian Government will provide that money\u201d. That is the type of friendship we have.\n\n2009 \u0d94\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dd9\u0dad\u0ddd\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 20 461 462\n\nAccording to the studies done, because of the deep wells that have been sunk in the North, now the water is getting mixed with saline causing a threat to agriculture. Some of the experts from the UK told us that because of the 30-year war, agriculture was not developed fast enough, they could just manage with the water level and the water available. But, in the future, when you go for extended agriculture we will have to seriously tackle this problem of salinity and hard water in the Northern Province. Let us face that together. Let us do that for the Northern farmers without always talking only about conflict, only about differences. Some of the differences are perfectly all right. Democratically, those differences must exist, but we have a huge area, Hon. Members, where we can work together to see that there is rapid growth. So, what we are trying to do is, on one side, to clean up our accounts regarding the expenditure of the war. For some years we will have to do that because we cannot run without funds."
  },
