    "chunk_text": "We continue to engage with the international community on a range of issues of mutual concern relating to the IDPs, resettlement and livelihood projects. Our engagement has included a series of meetings and\n\nThe resettlement of persons in their original areas of habitation and the resultant decrease in numbers in the IDPs to less than 250,000 is being appreciated by many quarters. The issuance of IDs to over 160,000 persons and the completion of registration of all IDPs over 12 years have been noted. We are confident that the targets set for clearance of 58,000 for resettlement by end October will be met. Dry rations and an allowance for the reconstruction of shelter for the returnees have been provided.\n\nThe notable progress made in the health sector with the reduction of the annual mortality rate to less than 4.4 per 1,000 in the welfare centres in Vavuniya, which is compatible with any other part of the country, symbolizes the significant achievement in stabilization of the health facilities for the IDPs.\n\nAlmost 40,000 children are attending classes in welfare centres. The Government has facilitated 1,187 students to sit for the GCE (Advanced Level) Examination in August this year. This reflects the emphasis the Government places on the long-term welfare of the present IDPs. The fact that 166 of them were LTTE surrendees needs to be appreciated.\n\nOur interlocutors have also been informed of the contingency plan and flood preparedness to face the imminent North-East monsoon rains. The construction and improvement of the storm water drainage system in Vavuniya by the RDA and the District Road Development Authority, the Sri Lanka Army with the partnership of international organizations have also to be noted. The fact that drainage facilities in Zones 1 and 2 have been completed is appreciated. Over 50 per cent of the work in the other zones has also been completed, except Zone 7, where work is to begin very soon.\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dd9\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0"
  },
