    "md5": "7d01f3b8db75133f8bed74e7e832333a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2316,
    "chunk_text": "Our interlocutors have also been informed of the contingency plan and flood preparedness to face the imminent North-East monsoon rains. The construction and improvement of the storm water drainage system in Vavuniya by the RDA and the District Road Development Authority, the Sri Lanka Army with the partnership of international organizations have also to be noted. The fact that drainage facilities in Zones 1 and 2 have been completed is appreciated. Over 50 per cent of the work in the other zones has also been completed, except Zone 7, where work is to begin very soon.\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dd9\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dd9\u0dbb\u0ddd\u0dc4\u0dd2\u0dad \u0dd9\u0db6\u0ddd\u0dd9\u0d9c\u0ddc\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0d9c\u0db8 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf ]\n\n637 638\n\nOn de-mining which is a prerequisite for resettlement of IDPs, we have articulated Sri Lanka\u2019s commitment to intensify de-mining. We have made the international community aware that it is the Government of Sri Lanka, through the expertise of the Sri Lanka Army, that has carried out over 70 per cent of de-mining. \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dd9\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0255 \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0b95\u0bc1\u1fa8\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bbe\u0bb3\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (Mr. Deputy Chairman of Committees) \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d87\u0db8\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db1\u0dd2, \u0dad\u0dc0 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0da9\u0dd2\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dca \u0d85\u0dc0\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dca \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dd9\u0dbb\u0ddd\u0dc4\u0dd2\u0dad \u0dd9\u0db6\u0ddd\u0dd9\u0d9c\u0ddc\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0d9c\u0db8 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u1f97\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bc7\u0bb0\u0bbe\u0bb9\u0bbf\u0ba4 \u0bc7\u0baa\u0bbe\u0bc6\u0b95\u0bbe\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0b95\u0bae) (The Hon. Rohitha Bogollagama) \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dd9\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0255 \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db1\u0dd2, \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0da9\u0dd2 \u0dad\u0dd4\u0db1\u0d9a\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dca \u0d89\u0dc0\u0dbb \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0db1\u0dc0\u0dcf.\n\nThe fact that the Government has disbursed large amount of funds to secure equipment for a speedier, mechanized de-mining process symbolizes the Government\u2019s commitment to de-mining and resettlement. In our interactions, we have emphasized particularly to those who call for a speedy resettlement, the need for tangible assistance in the de-mining process. Some have responded and the responses of others are pending. The certification by the UNHCR that the area is safe is a basic prerequisite before any resettlement can take place in an area. This is a rule strictly followed by the Government for the safety of our people."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2000s",
    "doc_id": "2009-10-21-2009-10-21",
    "num": "2009-10-21",
    "date_str": "2009-10-21",
    "description": "Hansard of October 21, 2009",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/PUBDOC2397_document.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2009-10-21-2009-10-21-0119",
    "chunk_index": 119,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "eca9c5af475d8444dec1013dc74b98a4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2282,
    "chunk_text": "The fact that the Government has disbursed large amount of funds to secure equipment for a speedier, mechanized de-mining process symbolizes the Government\u2019s commitment to de-mining and resettlement. In our interactions, we have emphasized particularly to those who call for a speedy resettlement, the need for tangible assistance in the de-mining process. Some have responded and the responses of others are pending. The certification by the UNHCR that the area is safe is a basic prerequisite before any resettlement can take place in an area. This is a rule strictly followed by the Government for the safety of our people.\n\nNow, I will move on to another very important area in terms of the GSP Plus.\n\n\u0db1\u0dd2\u0dd9\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0255 \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0b95\u0bc1\u1fa8\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bbe\u0bb3\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (Mr. Deputy Chairman of Committees) \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf\u0d9c\u0dad \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dd9\u0dbb\u0ddd\u0dc4\u0dd2\u0dad \u0dd9\u0db6\u0ddd\u0dd9\u0d9c\u0ddc\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0d9c\u0db8 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u1f97\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bc7\u0bb0\u0bbe\u0bb9\u0bbf\u0ba4 \u0bc7\u0baa\u0bbe\u0bc6\u0b95\u0bbe\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0b95\u0bae) (The Hon. Rohitha Bogollagama) \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dd9\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0255 \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db1\u0dd2, \u0db8\u0dcf \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0dc0 \u0d85\u0dc0\u0dc3\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dd9\u0dba\u0dca\u0daf\u0dd3 \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf\u0d9c\u0dad \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0db1\u0dc0\u0dcf.\n\nWith regard to the GSP Plus review process, on Monday, 19th October, 2009, the European Commission handed over to the Government of Sri Lanka its report on Sri Lanka\u2019s implementation of three of the 27 UN Conventions relevant to its GSP Plus benefits, which were of concern to the European Commission. The Note from the Directorate General for Trade of the European Commission forwarding the European Commission\u2019s report to the Mission of Sri Lanka in Brussels stated, \u201cThe Commission will now decide whether to propose a temporary withdrawal of the special incentive arrangement for sustainable development and good governance provided for under Council Regulation (EC) No. 732/2008\u201d. The Note goes on to add, \u201cIf the Government of Sri Lanka wishes to make any representations on this matter or specifically in relation to the Commission report in annex, it is kindly requested to bring these to the Commission\u2019s attention no later than 06th November, 2009\u2026..\u201d."
  },
