    "md5": "eeab88366d93bf1d2ac0b6d3a904dd03",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1789,
    "chunk_text": "With regard to the GSP Plus review process, on Monday, 19th October, 2009, the European Commission handed over to the Government of Sri Lanka its report on Sri Lanka\u2019s implementation of three of the 27 UN Conventions relevant to its GSP Plus benefits, which were of concern to the European Commission. The Note from the Directorate General for Trade of the European Commission forwarding the European Commission\u2019s report to the Mission of Sri Lanka in Brussels stated, \u201cThe Commission will now decide whether to propose a temporary withdrawal of the special incentive arrangement for sustainable development and good governance provided for under Council Regulation (EC) No. 732/2008\u201d. The Note goes on to add, \u201cIf the Government of Sri Lanka wishes to make any representations on this matter or specifically in relation to the Commission report in annex, it is kindly requested to bring these to the Commission\u2019s attention no later than 06th November, 2009\u2026..\u201d.\n\nWhile not co-operating with the process of \u201cinvestigation\u201d, the Government of Sri Lanka continued to engage with the European Commission on the issues of mutual interest through existing diplomatic channels, a fact acknowledged in the European Commission report. The Government of Sri Lanka for its part will continue to engage with the European institutions in keeping with the spirit of transparency and mutual respect that is appropriate to the historic and long-standing relationship between Europe and Sri Lanka.\n\nThe Government of Sri Lanka, within the joint Cabinet Sub-Committee appointed by His Excellency the President, will therefore closely study the European Commission report and consider ways and means of addressing the issues in our continuing pursuance of securing the GSP Plus facility."
  },
