    "chunk_size_bytes": 1760,
    "chunk_text": "Our interlocutors have also been informed of the contingency planning and flood preparedness in preparation for the Imminent North-East monsoon rains. Construction and improvement of the storm water drainage system in Vavuniya by the RDA and the District Road Development Authority, the Sri Lanka Army with the partnership of international organizations have also been noted. The fact that drainage facilities in zones 1 and 2 have been completed is being appreciated. Over 50 per cent of the work in the other zones have also been completed, except in zone7, where work is to begin very soon.\n\nthe safety of our people. The emphasis Sri Lanka has placed on the demining of the Rice Bowl in the Mannar District and the progress made in demining the region by the end of October, in time for the cultivation season, Demonstrated the commitment of the Government, not only to resettle the people in the region, but also to facilitate the return to their traditional livelihoods. The provision of land, plant material, fertilizer subsidies and equipment for the returnees is part of the additional financial commitment of the Government to our people. We have emphasized to our interlocutors that returning the people to demined areas is only one part of the challenge and that, from their end, tangible assistance is needed such as for construction of permanent shelter and developing of livelihood programmes in the area. We will continue to engage our interlocutors on this area of necessary assistance.\n\nThe sensitivity with which the Government is addressing the needs and difficulties of special categories of IDPs - the elderly, the clergy et al-by releasing them is also being appreciated. Up to now, over 10,000 have been considered under this programme."
