    "chunk_size_bytes": 1654,
    "chunk_text": "The sensitivity with which the Government is addressing the needs and difficulties of special categories of IDPs - the elderly, the clergy et al-by releasing them is also being appreciated. Up to now, over 10,000 have been considered under this programme.\n\nAs the Hon. Members are aware, for the short, medium and long-term development of the areas affected by the conflict, the infrastructure is vital. Our interlocutors have been informed of the progress made in the construction of the Kachcheries, Divisional and Pradeshiya Sabha buildings, schools and health facilities. The establishment of major government institutions including the BOI is being considered. The banking facilities including development banks have been established, which has been noted by the interlocutors.\n\nThe Hon. Members need to be aware that we have impressed on members of the international community the need to interdict anti-Sri Lanka activity by pro-LTTE groups which are inimical to Sri Lanka\u2019s national interest. We have impressed on them that just as much as calls are being made by the international community for reconciliation in Sri Lanka, the international community itself must also desist from permitting or turning a blind eye to continuing inimical action by pro-LTTE groups. We have emphasized that such inimical action will make the political processes in Sri Lanka and national reconciliation much more difficult and complex.\n\n( Rajaratnam) A Significant development was seen in the area of the LTTE\u2019s financing network. An individual named Raj Rajaratnam has been charged in the US on 16th October relating to insider trading involving hedge funds."
