    "chunk_text": "1. Mr. T.R. Baalu, former Indian Minister for Shipping and Transport and DMK Parliamentary Group Leader in the Lok Sabha (Lower House) 2. Mr. A.K.S. Vijayan, DMK MP in the Lok Sabha 3. Mr. T.K.S. Elangovan, DMK Lok Sabha MP 4. Ms. J. Helen Davidson, DMK Lok Sabha MP 5. Ms. Kanimozhi Karunanidhi, DMK Rajya Sabha MP (Upper House) and daughter of Hon. M. Karunanidhi, Chief Minister of Tamil Nadu 6. Mr. Thol. Thirumaavalavan, Viduthalai Chiruthaikal Katchchi (VCK) Lok Sabha MP 7. Mr. N.S.V. Chitthan, Congress Lok Sabha MP\n\n8. Mr. S. Alagiri, Congress Lok Sabha MP 9. Dr. E.M. Sudarsana Nachiappan, Congress Rajya Sabha MP 10. Mr. J.M. Haroon Rashid, Congress Lok Sabha\n\na. They were able to move freely and interact with the people accommodated at the welfare villages without any restrictions whatsoever. b. They were able to see for themselves the reality\n\nof the situation and observe the facilities provided and how the Government machinery is working in the interest of the IDPs. c. The people have, naturally, expressed their desire to return to their areas of residence, which is also the wish of the Government of Sri Lanka. d. The Government of Sri Lanka manifested its\n\ncommitment to act in a spirit of transparency. The Government moreover in opening the welfare villages for scrutiny, demonstrated that the authorities have nothing to hide or to be ashamed of, since they are acting in good faith. The visit and its outcome may be viewed with dismay and disappointment by pro-LTTE elements across the world, which have been thriving by criticizing the Government of Sri Lanka. The visit has been successful in debunking the criticism against the Government of Sri Lanka. The confirmation that a large number of the IDPs would be resettled in the coming weeks, would also be a blow to the pro-LTTE lobbies.\n\n[\u0baa\u0bbf.\u0baa. 1.02]\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dd9\u0dc3\u0ddc\u0dbd\u0db8\u0db1\u0dca \u0dc3\u0dd6. \u0dc3\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u1f97\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bc6\u0b9a\u0bbe\u0bb2\u0bae\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0bc2. \u0b9a\u0bbf\u0bb1\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd) (The Hon. Soloman S. Cyril)"
