    "chunk_size_bytes": 2393,
    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dd9\u0dbb\u0ddd\u0dc4\u0dd2\u0dad \u0dd9\u0db6\u0ddd\u0dd9\u0d9c\u0ddc\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0d9c\u0db8 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dd9\u0daf\u0dca\u0dc1 \u0d9a\u0da7\u0dba\u0dd4\u0dad\u0dd4 \u0d85\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad\u0255\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf)\n\n(\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u1f97\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bc7\u0bb0\u0bbe\u0bb9\u0bbf\u0ba4 \u0bc7\u0baa\u0bbe\u0bc6\u0b95\u0bbe\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0b95\u0bae - \u0bc6\u0bb5\u0bb3\u0bbf\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u1fa4 \u0bb5\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bc8\u0bae\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0bb0\u0bcd)\n\n(The Hon. Rohitha Bogollagama - Minister of Foreign Affairs)\n\nThat is all right. You go ahead.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dd9\u0dbb\u0ddd\u0dc4\u0dd2\u0dad \u0dd9\u0db6\u0ddd\u0dd9\u0d9c\u0ddc\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0d9c\u0db8 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u1f97\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bc7\u0bb0\u0bbe\u0bb9\u0bbf\u0ba4 \u0bc7\u0baa\u0bbe\u0bc6\u0b95\u0bbe\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0b95\u0bae) (The Hon. Rohitha Bogollagama)\n\nHon. Speaker, I am extremely happy that my learned and good Friend, the Hon. Ravi Karunanayake raised this matter. In fact, I was thinking of raising that as a matter of Privilege because today\u2019s \u201cThe Island\u201d newspaper has stated, \"An authoritative government official\" but they have not mentioned the name. I was wondering who said this because they have failed to state the name of the official or any other person of the Government who has disputed what I stated on the Floor of this House the day before yesterday. Therefore, it is irresponsible journalism that has been practised by this particular newspaper from which the Hon. Ravi Karunanayake has quoted. I now wonder for a moment whether this is a plan to raise this matter before the August Assembly today. I stand by what I have stated the day before yesterday, that we have submitted our claim in terms of the Legal Continental Shelf, properly and at the right time to the authorities concerned.\n\nSecondly, we are not going to claim any Indian territory unless we negotiate in terms of the seabed rights, even if it is touching some of our boundaries. This is what I stated very clearly and emphatically the day before yesterday; that if there are any boundaries that are touching or overlapping one another, that will be a matter for bilateral negotiations between India and Sri Lanka. I stand by what I said and would like \u201cThe Island\u201d newspaper to correct the statement that they have published and I would seek a direction from the Hon. Speaker to the newspaper concerned to reflect correctly what I have stated on the Floor of this House.\n\nThank you. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd2 \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u1f97\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb0\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u1f9e\u0ba3\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake)"
  },
