    "md5": "b7e5add9a9ee22a56f9fc30cde84e4c8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1773,
    "chunk_text": "Bismillahir Rahmanir Raheem. Nahumaduhu Salli ala Vanusalli Rasoolihil Kareem Venerable Presiding Member, I thank you for the op-portunity extended to me to participate in the Debate on the extension of the state of Emergency. Sri Lanka\u2019s post-independent electoral system offers few mechanisms through which the minorities can protect their rights against the majority, thereby ensuring the majority-dominated governments to remain in power. The system of territorial representation gives the majority parties a two-thirds of the government seats whereas the upcountry Tamils, the Northern and the Eastern Tamils were defran-chised way back in 1948. State-sponsored terrorism and large-scale violation of human rights, the results of the state of emergency in Sri Lanka, can be attributed to the country's anti-terrorist legislations, such as the Public Security Ordinance, the Prevention of Terrorism Act and the Emergency Regulations. These laws enable political and security officials at all levels to participate in an il-\n\nVenerable Presiding Member, during a state of emer-gency, the President may enforce Emergency Regulations to secure the public order of the State. While the PSO and the PTA bestow powers on the President, the Emer-gency Regulations are renewed monthly to further clar-ify and specify the tactics to be used by the Government to maintain law and order and to suppress the opponents.\n\nMoving on to the suppression of freedom of speech, the censoring of the press has deprived the Sri Lankan and international community of information regarding un-folding violence in the country. Regulation 14 seeks to limit the voice of the people who have no other means of rallying round for national and international support than through public awareness."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2000s",
    "doc_id": "2009-11-06-2009-11-06",
    "num": "2009-11-06",
    "date_str": "2009-11-06",
    "description": "Hansard of November 06, 2009",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
