    "md5": "09cfd07ab8916734f4eb3fdff8606d2d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2198,
    "chunk_text": "Moving on to the suppression of freedom of speech, the censoring of the press has deprived the Sri Lankan and international community of information regarding un-folding violence in the country. Regulation 14 seeks to limit the voice of the people who have no other means of rallying round for national and international support than through public awareness.\n\nWith regard to the police in this country, Venerable Pre-siding Member, there was a time when the people of this country had friendly police. Today the police is no longer people-friendly. Earlier, police officers were granted promo-tions on the basis of their years of service and transfers were granted on the number of years served in a particular police station. Those kind of promotions and installation of new officers are not being made by the Department of Police to-day, because it is highly politicized.\n\nThe delay in the formation of the National Police Com-mission deprives police officers of their legitimate right to\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dd9\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0 1197 1198\n\npromotions and transfers. There was a time when recom-mendations were made by the SSPs to the DIGs, who in turn passed it on to the senior DIGs, and finally, the IGP sum-mons those high officers for a meeting and approves the recommendations. Where are those recommendations? To-day, the recommendation of the politician is the main ne-cessity to transfer a police officer from one corner to an-other. Therefore, I would like to state that according to the Seventeenth Amendment to the Constitution, the National Police Commission is a must in this country. As you know, in the last Western Provincial Council Election, the police were really not interested in policing the area. In some areas, underworld people were used to - \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0ba4\u0bc8\u0bb2\u0bc8\u0bae\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u1fa0\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Presiding Member) \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf, \u0dd9\u0db8\u0ddc\u0dd9\u0dc4\u0ddc\u0dad\u0d9a\u0dca \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0dca\u0dc1\u0db6\u0dca\u0daf \u0dc0\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc0\u0dd3. \u0db4\u0dd4\u0dad\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dc3\u0dd2\u0d9c\u0dcf\u0db8\u0db1\u0dd3 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0d85\u0db0\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0dbb\u0dab \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dd9\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0255 \u0d85\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad\u0255\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf )"
  },
