0b8e\u0bae\u0bcd. \u0b87\u0bae\u0bbe\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. R.M. Imam) For the sake of politics he is not doing anything. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba \u0dc3\u0dbb\u0dad\u0dca \u0d85\u0db8\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dd4\u0d9c\u0db8 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u1f97\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b95\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf \u0b9a\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0b85\u1f99\u1f94\u0b95\u0bae) (The Hon. (Dr.) Sarath Amunugama) The problem is this. I do not know about your home and home matters. But what has happened is, as far as the Government is concerned, we are trying to promote them to go back. There are a lot of international agencies also who are willing to contribute to that. But now what has happened, Hon. Member? I was the Minister in charge of that some years ago, so I can tell you what has happened. There are some refugees in Puttalam who do not want to go back. They have got themselves adjusted there. Some of their children are going to schools in Puttalam. So, it is a complex problem. That is what I am trying to say."
