    "chunk_text": "\u0dbb\u0dcf\u0da2\u0255 \u0d86\u0dbb\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dc2\u0d9a,\u0db8\u0dc4\u0da2\u0db1 \u0d86\u0dbb\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dc2\u0dcf\u0dc0, \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dba \u0dc4\u0dcf \u0dc3\u0dcf\u0db8\u0dba \u0db4\u0dd2\u0dc5\u0dd2\u0db6\u0db3 \u0d85\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad\u0255\u0dcf\u0d82\u0dc1\u0dba\n\n\u0d85\u0d82\u0d9a 15/5, \u0db6\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0daf\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dc2 \u0db8\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0dad, \u0dd9\u0d9a\u0ddc\u0dc5\u0db9 03, \u0dc1\u0dd3 \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dc0. \u0baa\u0bbe\u1f90\u0b95\u0bbe\u0baa\u0bcd\u1f97, \u0bc6\u0baa\u0bbe\u1f90\u0bae\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd \u0baa\u0bbe\u1f90\u0b95\u0bbe\u0baa\u0bcd\u1f97, \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u1f99\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b92\u1fa8\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0baa\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0bbf\u0baf\n\n\u0b85\u0bc8\u0bae\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0bc1 \u0b87\u0bb2. 15/5, \u0baa\u0bbe\u0bb2\u0ba4\u0b95\u0bcd\u0bb7 \u0bae\u0bbe\u0bb5\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0bc8\u0ba4, \u0bc6\u0b95\u0bbe\u1fa8\u0bae\u0bcd\u1f97 03, \u0b87\u0bb2\u0b99\u0bcd\u0bc8\u0b95 MINISTRY OF DEFENCE, PUBLIC SECURITY, LAW &\n\ndefence.lk \u0daf\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dba 20 August, 2009 \u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b95\u0ba4\u0bbf Date Commander of the Army\n\nProcurement of Military Items from M/s Ploy Technologies, Inc. China\n\nThis refers to your letter No. G/Plans/71(48) dated 12.08.2009 2. The Secretary / Defence has directed not to accept the consignment referred in the above letter which is due to arrive at Colombo port on 20th August 2009 [L. Liyanagama], Chief Accountant, For Secretary / Defence, Public security, Law & Order. Copy to MGO Branch Dte to Plans Minute No. : MOD/09/038/Army dated 11.06.2009\n\nMINUTES OF THE MEETING OF THE STANDING CABINET APPOINTED PROCUREMENT COMMITTEE (SCAPC) - JUNE\n\n11TH, 2009 AT 4.15 P.M. Members Mr. Lalith Weeratunga, Secretary to H. E. the President - Chairman Mr. Gotabaya Rajapaksa, RWP, RSP, psc - Member Secretary, Ministry of Defence, Public Secretary, Law and Order Mr. Sumith Abeysinghe, Secretary to the Treasury - Member Mr. S. Amarasekara, Secretary, Ministry, of Highways & Road Development - Member In attendance Maj. Gen JJPST Liyange, Master Genral Ordance/SL Army (Representing the Commander of the Sri Lanka Army) Brig. NUMMW Senanayaka, Director Plans/SL Army\n\nPURCHASE OF 30,000 NOS 122 MM MBRL ROCKETS FOR RM-70\n\nGRAD OF THE SRI LANKA ARMY (Extension for the LC and last date of shipment) 1. The SCAPC which met on 11.06.2009 at the Office of the Secretary/\n\nDeference, Public Security, Law & Order considered the letter dated 20.05.2009 sent by the Commander of the Army with regard to the procurement of 30,000 Nos. 122 mm MBRL Rockets for the SL Army and the Technical Evaluation Committee (TEC) report dated 08.12.2008 annexed thereto. 2. The following we observed by the SCAPC-\n\n(a) Cabinet of Ministers vide Cabinet decision numbered"
