    "chunk_text": "Deference, Public Security, Law & Order considered the letter dated 20.05.2009 sent by the Commander of the Army with regard to the procurement of 30,000 Nos. 122 mm MBRL Rockets for the SL Army and the Technical Evaluation Committee (TEC) report dated 08.12.2008 annexed thereto. 2. The following we observed by the SCAPC-\n\n(a) Cabinet of Ministers vide Cabinet decision numbered\n\n6 - PL 004619 - (2009/12)\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dd9\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0 1551 1552\n\n2. The following were observed by the SCAPC -\n\n(a) Cabinet of Ministers vide Cabinet decision numbered CM/08/0985/305/042/TBR dated 12.06.2008 has granted approval to procure 30,000 Nos. 122mm MBRL Rockets for RM - 70 GRAD of the SL Army form M/s LL&TL) at a total C&F cost of USD 6,750,000.00\n\n(b) The approved unit cost of a 122mm MBRL rocket is USD 225.00 on C&F basis. However, the supplier has now reported that they are unable to maintain the initial quoted price due to the circumstances and events that delayed in obtaining the Export permit. Accordingly, the revised unit cost now would be USD 230.00 on FOB basis or USD 323.00 on C&F basis.\n\n(c) Further, the supplier highlights that the additional cost for transport and the depreciation of US Dollar against Slovak Koruna were badly affected to this price escalation.\n\n(d) M/s LL&TL has reported that this price enhancement occurred due to volatility in the market arising from;\n\ni. Wide publicity given by the media for the on going war in Sri Lanka against terrorists. ii. New demand for similar products from Georgia, Kenya and Sudan.\n\niii. Awareness by the supplier the purchase of 10,000 Nos. MBRLs from M/s STV, Czech Republic at a FOB cost of USD 270.00 and CIF cost of USD 347.60 per unit.\n\n(e) Commander of the Army who awaits the goods urgently reports that the revised price is reasonable when compared with the prices of the other suppliers for the same producet. Further, he highlights that they have no alternative source to satisfy above requirement at present."
