    "chunk_text": "(e) Commander of the Army who awaits the goods urgently reports that the revised price is reasonable when compared with the prices of the other suppliers for the same producet. Further, he highlights that they have no alternative source to satisfy above requirement at present.\n\n(g) In view of the above facts, Commander of the Army strongly recommends to procure 30,000 Nos 122 mm MBRL rockets for RM - 70 GRAD of the SL Army from M/s Way Industries a. s., Slovakia at a revised unit cost of USD 230.00 on FOB basis or USD 323.00 on C&F basis.\n\n3. Considering the requirement and the recommendations made by the Commander of the Army, the SCAPC recommends to the Cabinet of Ministers to procure 30,000 Nos 122 mm MBRL rockets for RM - 70 GRAD of the SL Army from M/s Way Industries a. s., Slovakia at a revised unit cost of USD 323.00 on C&F basis. Accordingly, total cost now should read as USD 9,690,000.00 on C&F basis.\n\nLalith Weeratunga Gotabaya Rajapaksa RWP,RSP, psc Secretary to H. E. the President Secretary, Ministry of Defence, Chairman Public Security, Law & Order Meber\n\nS. Amarasekara Sumith Abeysinghe Secretary, Ministry of Highways & Secretary to the Treasury Road Development Member Member\n\n2009 \u0dd9\u0daf\u0dc3\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 08 1553 1554\n\n\u0dc1\u0dd3 \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u0dba\u0dd4\u0daf\u0dca\u0db0 \u0dc4\u0db8\u0dd4\u0daf\u0dcf \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dc3\u0dca\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dba, \u0dad\u0dd0. \u0dd9\u0db4. 553, \u0dd9\u0d9a\u0ddc\u0dc5\u0db9 \u0b87\u0bb2\u0b99\u0bcd\u0bc8\u0b95\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0bc8\u0bb0\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc8\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0bc8\u0bb2\u0bc8\u0bae\u0baf\u0b95\u0bae\u0bcd, \u0ba4. \u0bc6\u0baa. 553, \u0bc6\u0b95\u0bbe\u1fa8\u0bae\u0bcd\u1f97 SRI LANKA ARMY HEADQUARTERS, P. O. BOX 553, COLOMBO G/Plans/17/01/MBRL/2007/02 (65) Secretary Ministry of Defence 20 May 2009 PURCHASE OF 122 MM MBRL ROCKETS - 30,000 NOS Reference : A. Army Headquarters letter G/Plans/17/01/MBRL/2007/02(61) dated 06 May 2009.\n\nB. Army Headquarters letter G/Plans/17/01/MBRL/2007/02(62) dated 07 May 2009."
  },
