    "md5": "45c5c5a9f69a8556cc097b6dccb92fa6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1889,
    "chunk_text": "In Valikamam North in the Jaffna District, the people who were displaced as far back as 1989 and 1990 on account of the High Security Zone - for almost for the past 20 years, two long decades - have not been able to live on their lands. Twenty eight thousand families consisting of about 100,000 people were displaced from the High Security Zone. The vast majority of them, about 60 per cent, were people depending on agriculture on land in the High Security Zone. There were 45 Grama Sevaka Divisions covered by the High Security Zone, an entire territory of 59.5 square kilometres, about 60 square\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da9\u0db6\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dca. \u0da9\u0dd3. \u0dd9\u0da2\u0dca. \u0dd9\u0dc3\u0dd9\u0db1\u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dad\u0dca\u0db1 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2009 \u0dd9\u0daf\u0dc3\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 08 1573 1574\n\nWhen the President addressed the SLFP Convention that year, on the 04th of September, 2006, he said, \u201cOur armed forces have captured Sumpur for the welfare and benefit of the people living there.\u201d If Sampur has been captured for the benefit and welfare of the people living there, surely people must be able to go back to their lands. That is not happening,\n\nI want to urge that the High Security Zones be dismantled without further delay. In fact, I urge that the High Security Zones be dismantled before the forthcoming Presidential Election. At least the process of dismantling must commence before the Presidential Election and it must be completed before the Parliamentary Election. You cannot be keeping tens of thousands of people out of their residences and their agricultural land when there is no justification whatever any longer for these lands to be regarded as High Security Zones, because the LTTE is not there; the artillery is not there; there is no firing there; the entire territory is under your control and how can you justify their being High Security Zones? I do not think this situation can be allowed to continue."
  },
