    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/PUBDOC2447_document.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2009-12-08-2009-12-08-0172",
    "chunk_index": 172,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "77c3a3cfb330d95119e974c0f4fa41c3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1660,
    "chunk_text": "I want to urge that the High Security Zones be dismantled without further delay. In fact, I urge that the High Security Zones be dismantled before the forthcoming Presidential Election. At least the process of dismantling must commence before the Presidential Election and it must be completed before the Parliamentary Election. You cannot be keeping tens of thousands of people out of their residences and their agricultural land when there is no justification whatever any longer for these lands to be regarded as High Security Zones, because the LTTE is not there; the artillery is not there; there is no firing there; the entire territory is under your control and how can you justify their being High Security Zones? I do not think this situation can be allowed to continue.\n\nThese are challenges the Government must be prepared to face. I mean, things have been done in a way which seems to suggest that the Government has no serious commitment in regard to these matters. Things have been done in an ad hoc way - things have not been comprehensively planned and things have not been properly implemented - that is our complaint. So, Venerable Presiding Member, these are matters which we raise on the Floor of this House quite frequently, but nobody takes them too seriously.\n\nBut now with the elections in the offing, at least I hope that there will be a little more seriousness and that you will not fail in your duty to ensure that these people are not deprived any longer of their lands on which they would like to reside, on which they have lived for generations and centuries and on which they must carry on their cultivation and their occupation."
  },
