    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "5abd3e91bf7f392494db08eb98fa6686",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1727,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cGovernment is keen to see the revival of the political process in Sri Lanka, which will meet the legitimate interests and aspiration of all communities, including the Tamils and the Muslims, within the framework of a united Sri Lanka. Revival of such a political process and an inclusive dialogue would help bring the minority communities into the political mainstream. We have continued to emphasize to the Sri Lankan Government to put forward a meaningful devolution package \u2026.\u201d\n\n\u201cWe will remain engaged with them through this process of transition and reform.\u201d\n\nThat is the statement made by the Indian Minister of External Affairs in the Rajya Sabha when he spoke on the situation in the North-East. So, the Government is engaged in all these activities in the North-East, whether it is militarization, further militarization, not engaged in demilitarization, maintenance of High Security Zones, keeping out foreign governments and INGOs from the North-East when they can contribute very effectively and extensively to resettlement and rehabilitation in those areas. All this is happening because the Government is unable to come up with a political solution and the Government thinks that the military presence and militarization is inevitable in that situation.\n\nBefore I conclude, Venerable Presiding Member, I want to refer to a very serious act of vandalism that has occurred in the Trincomalee District very recently, in about the past two weeks. There was an ancient Sivan temple, Sir, said to have been established by the much venerated Hindu Munivar Agasthiar called the Agasthiar Sthapanam.\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d86\u0dbb\u0dca. \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dca\u0db4\u0db1\u0dca\u0daf\u0db1\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2009 \u0dd9\u0daf\u0dc3\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 08 1577 1578"
  },
