    "date_str": "2009-12-08",
    "description": "Hansard of December 08, 2009",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/PUBDOC2447_document.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2009-12-08-2009-12-08-0229",
    "chunk_index": 229,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "2f769490fb41a61fa9bec263ab7557fd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1971,
    "chunk_text": "But, the issue here is, the UNP. The UNP has no candidate and today they have a joint candidate or whom we term as a candidate who has been proposed -\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd3\u0dc0\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dca (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u1f97\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b89\u1fa0\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b92\u1f9e\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd) (An Hon. Member)\n\nA common candidate. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dd9\u0dbb\u0ddd\u0dc4\u0dd2\u0dad \u0dd9\u0db6\u0ddd\u0dd9\u0d9c\u0ddc\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0d9c\u0db8 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u1f97\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bc7\u0bb0\u0bbe\u0bb9\u0bbf\u0ba4 \u0bc7\u0baa\u0bbe\u0bc6\u0b95\u0bbe\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0b95\u0bae) (The Hon. Rohitha Bogollagama)\n\n2009 \u0dd9\u0daf\u0dc3\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 08 1617 1618\n\nestablishment of Sri Lanka, the sovereignty of our country? A person holding the office of the Army Commander or the Chief of Defence Staff of any country cannot - it is never done as a matter of principle and to maintain the integrity of that office - deal with other countries either privately or officially, unless it is done through the channels that are meant for such communication and such conduct. That is what we term as the protector of the State. The President or the defence establishment cannot deal with foreign embassies or foreign missions in any direct manner whilst visiting them in their premises. We have not had such instances.\n\nBut now, we are aware of such situations that have developed and there is concern, a reasonable fear that we maintain, that the country\u2019s territorial integrity and the sovereignty, to some extent have, have been undermined or have been exposed by some actions of this officer concerned. Where do you find an officer being permitted to be interrogated on foreign soil, an officer with whom privileged information is retained? If one has been conniving, it is a serious offence in terms of the country\u2019s Constitution and the legal system. Here is an instance where General Fonseka had been subjected to that type of conduct and this also brings to light to what extent the General concerned has undermined the sovereignty and the territorial integrity of our country."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2000s",
