    "description": "Hansard of December 08, 2009",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/PUBDOC2447_document.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2009-12-08-2009-12-08-0230",
    "chunk_index": 230,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "e22cbca0f8772516e0ad40c5ff93023a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2159,
    "chunk_text": "But now, we are aware of such situations that have developed and there is concern, a reasonable fear that we maintain, that the country\u2019s territorial integrity and the sovereignty, to some extent have, have been undermined or have been exposed by some actions of this officer concerned. Where do you find an officer being permitted to be interrogated on foreign soil, an officer with whom privileged information is retained? If one has been conniving, it is a serious offence in terms of the country\u2019s Constitution and the legal system. Here is an instance where General Fonseka had been subjected to that type of conduct and this also brings to light to what extent the General concerned has undermined the sovereignty and the territorial integrity of our country.\n\n\u0db1\u0dd2\u0dd9\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0255 \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Deputy Speaker)\n\nHon. Minister, your time is over.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dd9\u0dbb\u0ddd\u0dc4\u0dd2\u0dad \u0dd9\u0db6\u0ddd\u0dd9\u0d9c\u0ddc\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0d9c\u0db8 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u1f97\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bc7\u0bb0\u0bbe\u0bb9\u0bbf\u0ba4 \u0bc7\u0baa\u0bbe\u0bc6\u0b95\u0bbe\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0b95\u0bae) (The Hon. Rohitha Bogollagama)\n\nSir, give me only one more minute. Sir, I must also bring to your notice the concerns that have now been expressed in terms of our efforts. Today, we have made major improvement and progress in the settlement of the IDPs. The concerns that were expressed earlier have now subdued. They are much less because the international community has seen the positive action that is taking place in Sri Lanka with regard to the settlement of the IDPs . We have made vast progress and the tides that have been generated will only make it possible for the Tamil brotherhood to become part and parcel of normal life in the North.\n\nThen, in terms of the GSP concession, all the pessimism - and also to some extent the sarcasm - that have been expressed will not live long. Sri Lanka is confident and will be looking forward for the continuation of our engagement with the European Union and we will see how best that measurement will come into effect in terms of our engagement and Sri Lanka will not be a denied State."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2000s",
    "doc_id": "2009-12-08-2009-12-08",
    "num": "2009-12-08",
    "date_str": "2009-12-08",
    "description": "Hansard of December 08, 2009",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/PUBDOC2447_document.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2009-12-08-2009-12-08-0231",
    "chunk_index": 231,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "b4b15578d8ccaa7f5a3be2a5c2993f21",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2118,
    "chunk_text": "Then, in terms of the GSP concession, all the pessimism - and also to some extent the sarcasm - that have been expressed will not live long. Sri Lanka is confident and will be looking forward for the continuation of our engagement with the European Union and we will see how best that measurement will come into effect in terms of our engagement and Sri Lanka will not be a denied State.\n\n\u201cSri Lanka being endorsed at the recent summit to host the 2013 CHOGM on a proposal made by British Prime Minister Gordon Brown, is an important milestone in the consistent engagement of our country with the work of the Commonwealth. Since Australia and Mauritius had also offered to be host the CHOGM, Prime Minister Gordon Brown articulated the position that all three countries are equally qualified for this purpose. It was decided by the Commonwealth Heads of Government that Australia hosts CHOGM 2011 followed by Sri Lanka in 2013 and Mauritius in 2015. This consensual endorsement of Sri Lanka by the entire membership of the Commonwealth singularly demonstrates the acceptance of Sri Lanka\u2019s adherence to Commonwealth values and principles, with the country being a vibrant democracy.\u201d\n\nThe credit goes to President Mahinda Rajapaksa for having raised Sri Lanka\u2019s profile as the CHOGM will be held, for the first time in the independent history of Sri Lanka, in our country in 2013, which has been entirely endorsed by all the Heads of State of the Commonwealth countries, numbering 53.\n\nThank you, Sir. [\u0d85. \u0db7\u0dcf. 3.14] \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dd9\u0d9a\u0dca. \u0dc0\u0dd3. \u0dc3\u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0daf\u0255\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dad\u0dca\u0db1 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u1f97\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bc7\u0b95. \u0bb5\u0bbf. \u0b9a\u0bae\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4 \u0bb5\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baf\u0bbe\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba9) (The Hon. K.V. Samantha Vidyaratne) \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dd9\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0255 \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db1\u0dd2, \u0dc4\u0daf\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0dd2 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dba \u0dad\u0dc0\u0dad\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc3\u0d9a\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dca \u0daf\u0dd3\u0dbb\u0dca\u0d9d \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dd9\u0db8\u0dca \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u0daf\u0dd9\u0dba\u0dca \u0daf\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dd4 \u0daf\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dc0\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1\u0da7 \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0da9\u0dcf \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0ddd \u0dd9\u0dc0\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0d9a\u0dca \u0dbd\u0dd0\u0db6\u0dd3\u0db8 \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0db1\u0dca\u0db0\u0dd9\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca \u0dc3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0da7\u0dd4 \u0dc0\u0db1\u0dc0\u0dcf."
  },
